1 NOTE Tupac Amaru was made a high priest by Titu Cusi Yupanqui and was put in charge of his father's mummy and the sacred gold statue of Punchao that contained the ashes of the hearts of all of Tupac Amaru's deceased royal ancestors. Fr
2 CONC ancisco de Toledo declared war upon Vilacabamba on April 14 1572.
2 CONT He was dead set on ending the Yupanqui dynasty. He and his army destroyed the last independant Inca city. Martin Garcia de Loyola captured Tupac Amaru Yupanqui and his wife and child.
2 CONT He had promised them no harm would come to them. Again another Inca emperor was tried and convicted on trumped up charges. Tupac Amaru lived long enough to see his father's mummy burned and the sacred statue melted down. Tupac Ama
2 CONC ru was hung in an act of overt Regicide in Cuzco's main plaza.
2 CONT His descendant Tupac Amaru II born 19 March 1742 executed 1781 was responsible for leading a revolt against the Spanish rule. He and his family were captured. He was made to watch his wife, children and family get executed before 
2 CONC he was drawn and quartered in the same plaza in Cuzco that Tupac Amaru was exectued in. After Tupac Amaru I execution all the descendants of the royal Incas were sought out and scattered in exhile to Chile, Boliva and Mexico. No d
2 CONC oubt that many of them survived.
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT Cobo Bernabe, History of the New World, Bk 12.
