1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} RATSMITGLIED
2 CONT
2 CONT Nachrichten von einigen Ratsherren
2 CONT aus der Zorn Meixnerschen Chronik Seite 406
2 CONT von Elisabeth Zotz
2 CONT
2 CONT "..Mitglieder des Wormser Rates... Diese Handschrift wird im Stadtarchiv Worms verwhart...
2 CONT
2 CONT 1563 Bernhard Schlatt, Leinenkrämer sodann Holzhändler, starb ao. 92, 19.September.aetatis 52."
2 CONT
2 CONT __________________________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT City Museum, from the Lutheran cemetery
2 CONT
2 CONT Description
2 CONT
2 CONT Fragmentarily preserved grave monument of the Worms councillor and mayor Bernhard Schlatt, his wife Veronika née Birling and eight of their children. Lower southern stone on the east wall of the 4th niche of the cloister south win
2 CONC g, from the Lutheran cemetery.1) Lower or middle part of a larger monument made of reddish-yellow sandstone, whose death inscriptions (A,B) are lost. What has been preserved is a transverse rectangular fragment with a row of praye
2 CONC rs consisting of two adults on the outside, six youths, a girl and an infant on the inside, clothing and posture are each very uniform. Above the persons are their names or initials and, if necessary, a cross (C). The scene is fla
2 CONC nked by heraldic pilasters bearing inscriptions; four coats of arms and two inscriptions are still present.
2 CONT
2 CONT A and B according to Zorn-Meixner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dimensions: H.(erh.) 83,5, W. 138, Bu. 3.2-4 cm (C).
2 CONT
2 CONT Font(s): Kapitalis.
2 CONT
2 CONT A
2 CONT Anno. 1592. den 19. (novem)bre. the honorable and prudent Mr. Bernhard Schlatt, old Schulthes and (nd) of the constant councillor alhir, has fallen asleep in God.
2 CONT
2 CONT B
2 CONT Sodan(n) the virtuous Veronica Bilbenigerina) sein Ehlich haußfrau A(nn)o〈1596.〉 den 〈17t July〉 evenly secluded from this valley of misery, the same and betrayed a joyful resurrection to all of us God.
2 CONT
2 CONT C
2 CONT BERNHARD(VS)b) /SCHLAT · / VERONICA / BIERLINGERI(N)
2 CONT BARTH(OLOMEVS) · BER(NHARD) = CHRI(STOPH)c) · I(OHANN) · G(EORG) · AND(REAS)d) · I(OHANN) · I(ACOB) · I(OHANN) · C(HRISTOPH)e) / MARGRETHAf)
2 CONT
2 CONT Coat of arms inscriptions:
2 CONT [........] R (curved oblique beam, studded with lace, accompanied by rose at the bottom left), MEIEL; [........] R2), MARQVARTg)
2 CONT Comment
2 CONT
2 CONT The inscriptions A and B were not handed down by Zorn-Meixner with a single inscription carrier. However, since the persons are the same and the present fragment requires an addition to the coat of arms and death notices, both par
2 CONC ts have been pulled together here. It would be unusual for members of the bourgeois-Lutheran council families to have two memorial memorials, but it would be very easy to imagine dismantling a multi-part monument.
2 CONT
2 CONT The linen merchant and later timber merchant Bernhard Schlatt was elected to the Common Council in 1563 and to the Thirteen Council in 1573; he died at the age of 52.3) His wife Veronika was the daughter of Peter Birling. 4) The s
2 CONC ons Bernhard Christoph and Andreas were elected to the Common Council in 1590 and 1591.5) Bernhard Christoph in 1592 for his father also in the Council of Thirteen.6) Due to the occurrence of the coats of arms Meiel, Lisberg and M
2 CONC arquart shows the close family connection among Worms council families.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernhard Schlatt also worked as a private chronicler.7)
2 CONT
2 CONT Critical apparatus
2 CONT
2 CONT This is the case for Bierlingerin.
2 CONT Exaggerated capitals in all names.
2 CONT Christian Zorn-Meixner.
2 CONT Anor. ibid.
2 CONT Jo ibid. Ig.And.Jo. Wörner. The assignment of the names to the respective figures is not clear. According to the division proposed above, there is a small cross above the heads of Bernhard, Bartholomew, Johann Georg, Johann Jakob,
2 CONC  Johann Christoph and Margaretha.
2 CONT Lacks Zorn-Meixner.
2 CONT Mirror writing.
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Zorn-Meixner, in the east wall, 5th and 7th stone from the south.
2 CONT According to the coat of arms on the tombstone of Johann Christoph Marchard from 1617, cf. No. 647, it must be the coat of arms of Lisberg.
2 CONT Kraus, Quellen II 127 u. I 91.
2 CONT Ibid., I, 91.
2 CONT Ibid. II 129.
2 CONT Ibid., I, 92.
2 CONT See "Special Excerpts of Worms Things", StA Worms, Abt. 200 Nr. 24 u. Zorn-Meixner fol. 167v.
2 CONT Evidence
2 CONT
2 CONT Zorn-Meixner fol. 390v-391 Nos. 14 (A,B) and 16 (C).Wörner, Medieval Tombs 101 (C only).
