1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Merchant based in Florence, Italy. Consul of Spain in Florence in 1548. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Along with his brother Gonzalo Polanco Salinas, they were the house representatives (or "factores") of the Polanco family business in Florence and both belonged to the court of Cosimo I de Medici. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Palace of the Polancos in Florence was located in the center of the city on street Borgo Ognissanti and some of the burial slabs of the family representatives can be found in the Capilla de los Españoles and cloister in the Ch
2 CONC urch of Santa Maria Novella.
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanca, Gonzalez Talavera. "Presencia y mecenazgo español en la Florencia Medicea: de Cosme I a Fernando I (p 129 and 166)" (PDF). https://digibug.ugr.es/bitstream/handle/10481/19557/20082769.pdf?sequence=1&isAllowed=y
2 CONT
2 CONT GEI. "Diccionario de espiritualidad ignaciana, Volume 2 (p.1463) https://books.google.se/books?id=Bszl_HDhhz8C&pg=PA1463&dq=Luis+Gonzalo+Polanco+Florencia&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwi2qPnY_sbaAhXG_ywKHYN4DGMQ6AEILjAB#v=onepage&q=Luis%2
2 CONC 0Gonzalo%20Polanco%20Florencia&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT Carteggio universale di Cosimo I de Medici: (1549-1551) Mediceo del Principato, filze 392-403A https://books.google.se/books?id=xXgsAAAAYAAJ&dq=Luis+Polanco+Firenze&focus=searchwithinvolume&q=Polanco
2 CONT
2 CONT Testament of his father Gregorio de Polanco in 1546 (p. 27) https://riubu.ubu.es/bitstream/handle/10259.4/1588/0211-8998_n172_p001-029.pdf?sequence=1&isAllowed=y
