1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Spanish merchant and financier, member of a family of merchants originally from Burgos, possibly of Jewish origin, who had commercial offices in different cities of Western Europe.
2 CONT
2 CONT He maintained economic links with the powerful German families Fúcar and Bélzar. He managed a commercial house first in Portugal and then in Spain, dedicated to the traffic of different merchandise, mainly spices, with which he fi
2 CONC nanced numerous expeditions, among others, the first to reach the Río de la Plata (1511-1512) and that of Magallanes and Elcano (1519-1522), the first to circumnavigate the globe.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a factor of the Casa de Contratación de la Especies de La Coruña and councilor of Burgos. He developed an important relationship with the Emperor Charles V of the Holy Roman Empire. Thanks to the capital that he accumulated
2 CONC  as an entrepreneur, he became the monarch's lender. He also knew how to operate as his informant and spy thanks to the international links he had developed as a merchant.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crist%C3%B3bal_de_Haro
